# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on both macOS (LF) and Windows. Several tests
# READ SOURCE FILES and match on multi-line patterns — e.g. app_test.go looks
# for "\n}\n" to find a function's end, and the frontend tests slice settings.js
# between "addField(\n    '..." markers. Under Windows' default
# core.autocrlf=true those files are checked out with CRLF, the "\n"-based
# patterns stop matching, and the tests fail (one panics on a negative slice)
# on Windows only while passing on the Mac. Forcing LF for text files on every
# platform makes the checkout, and therefore the tests and tooling, identical
# everywhere.
#
# git auto-detects text vs binary (text=auto); eol=lf pins the ending for the
# text ones. Known binary assets are marked explicitly so their bytes are never
# touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.zip  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.syso binary
*.pdf  binary
